# Travel and Expense Policy

**Document Type:** Corporate Policy
**Authority Level:** 1 (Authoritative)
**Policy Number:** POL-003
**Effective Date:** January 1, 2025
**Last Reviewed:** January 2026
**Owner:** Chief Financial Officer
**Classification:** Internal

---

## Purpose

This policy establishes guidelines for business travel and expense reimbursement, ensuring cost-effective travel while maintaining employee comfort and safety.

---

## Scope

This policy applies to all Nexus Industries employees and contractors traveling on company business or incurring business expenses.

---

## General Principles

1. **Business Purpose:** All travel must have a valid business purpose
2. **Cost Consciousness:** Choose economical options without sacrificing safety or productivity
3. **Advance Planning:** Book travel 14+ days ahead when possible for best rates
4. **Approval:** Obtain required approvals before travel
5. **Documentation:** Keep receipts for all expenses over $25

---

## Travel Approval

### Approval Requirements

| Travel Type | Approval Required |
|-------------|-------------------|
| Domestic (<3 days) | Manager |
| Domestic (3+ days) | Director |
| International | VP + Division Travel Coordinator |
| High-Risk Countries | VP + Security + Legal |
| Customer Site | Manager |

### Booking Requirements

- Use corporate travel portal (Concur/SAP)
- Book at least 7 days in advance (14 preferred)
- Select preferred vendors when available
- Document business purpose

---

## Air Travel

### Class of Service

| Flight Duration | Standard | Executive (VP+) |
|-----------------|----------|-----------------|
| <4 hours | Economy | Economy |
| 4-8 hours | Economy | Premium Economy |
| >8 hours | Premium Economy | Business Class |
| Redeye/Connecting at destination | Premium Economy | Business Class |

**Exceptions Requiring VP Approval:**
- Business class for non-executives
- First class (not permitted except with CEO approval)
- Non-preferred airlines

### Booking Guidelines

| Requirement | Standard |
|-------------|----------|
| Advance Booking | 14+ days = best rate |
| Preferred Airlines | United, Delta, American (domestic) |
| Fare Type | Lowest logical airfare |
| Changes/Cancellations | Business reason required |
| Frequent Flyer | Personal use permitted |

---

## Lodging

### Hotel Standards

| Employee Level | Per Night Limit (US) |
|----------------|---------------------|
| Individual Contributor | $200 |
| Manager/Director | $250 |
| VP+ | $350 |
| High-Cost Cities (NYC, SF, London) | +50% |

**Preferred Hotels:** Marriott, Hilton, Hyatt (corporate rates available)

### Guidelines

- Book standard room unless medical need
- Select hotels near meeting location
- Use corporate rate codes
- Incidentals are employee responsibility (movies, minibar)

---

## Ground Transportation

### Policy by Type

| Type | When to Use | Limit |
|------|-------------|-------|
| Rental Car | Remote locations, multiple stops | Mid-size max |
| Taxi/Rideshare | Airport, short trips | Reasonable |
| Public Transit | Available and efficient | Encouraged |
| Personal Vehicle | Local travel | IRS rate ($0.67/mile) |

### Rental Car Guidelines

- Mid-size vehicle maximum (full-size with VP approval)
- Decline insurance (corporate coverage)
- Fuel up before return
- Preferred vendors: Enterprise, National, Hertz

